cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "video-editing: an agent skill for post-ready short-form explainer videos"
message: "If you use this skill or build on it, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The video-editing-skill authors"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
abstract: >-
  An agent skill and toolkit that produce short-form vertical explainer
  videos end to end, to a standard where the person who commissioned the
  video finds nothing to fix: topic selection, research with provenance,
  fact verification, script, synthetic narration timed to the word, a
  composed music bed, Remotion animation in a light house style, captions,
  covers, rendering, automated QA gates, one exhaustive independent review
  by named sub-agents, the fix loop, release staging and the read-back
  after posting. Every rule records the production failure that produced
  it and the check that now catches it.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - agent-skills
  - claude-code
  - cursor
  - codex
  - remotion
  - video-production
  - short-form-video
  - explainer-video
  - quality-assurance
